Immediate needs
---------------
fwdsp: Keep GStreamer strictly isolated in external fwdsp subprocesses
  - NEVER link or initialize GStreamer in rrclient/rrserver/audio.engine or other core code.
    User-configurable pipelines can crash or hang; a bad pipeline must not take
    down the client, server, or independent PCM mixer.
  - TODO: add per-pipeline crash/restart rate limiting with exponential backoff,
    a bounded restart budget, and a circuit breaker that suspends repeatedly
    failing pipelines until an operator explicitly re-enables them.
  - Expose suspended state, reason, crash count, and a manual re-enable action
    in the UI and logs. Ensure clean shutdowns do not count as crashes.

librrprotocol: Protocol versions and capabilities
  - we should support talking to older stuff now by degrading to their capabilities

rrclient: Support for multiple theme files in ~/.config/rustyrig/themes/ and /etc/rustyrig/themes/

librustyaxe: Ensure full separation from rrclient/rrserver/*

rrclient: Make audit/ptt logs available for all connected servers (dropdown instead of relying on status tab selection)

rrclient: Make hotkeys configurable

rrserver: Add support for SCRAM gpio

* Move all socket code out of librrprotocol
  - It needs to go into client and server code
    - client glib/wslay/$webtransport or libmongoose (embedded)
    - server glib/wslay/$webtransport OR libmongoose (embedded)

*: Rotator/amp/ATU support
   - backend.internal, backend.hamlib, and backend.network based

librustyaxe: logger - extend log.level so its allows throttling like log.level=*:info,event:crazy@10,6 to allow 10 messages in 6 seconds?

* WebTransport support
  - https://github.com/ngtcp2/ngtcp2/
  - https://github.com/ngtcp2/nghttp3/
  - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebTransport#examples

* Deferred WWV/WWVH time-source worker: see doc/wwv-time-decoder-plan.md.
  Not required for monotonic protocol RTT; implement after beta transport/state work.

rrbridge: More connectors!
